snp3.4:16.1 starts: Those with well-restrained minds,
snp3.4:16.2 starts: straight as a shuttle:
snp3.4:16.3 starts: To them, at the right time,
snp3.4:16.4 starts: you should bestow an offering,
snp3.4:35.1 starts: The Buddha:
snp3.4:35.2 starts: whose mind is limpid,
snp3.4:35.3 starts: whose sloth is dispelled
snp3.4:35.4 starts: —fully released from sensuality—
snp3.5:25.1 starts: He—devoid of passion, subduing aversion,
snp3.5:25.2 starts: developing a mind of goodwill
snp3.5:25.3 starts: day & night, continually heedful—
snp3.5:25.4 starts: should pervade all the directions
snp3.6:13.1 starts: The Buddha:
snp3.6:13.3 starts: by means of the path accomplished by himself,
snp3.6:13.4 starts: having abandoned becoming & non-becoming,
snp3.6:13.5 starts: having fulfilled [the task],
snp3.6:16.1 starts: Having evaluated all theories,
snp3.6:16.2 starts: the wandering-on,
snp3.6:16.3 starts: having done away with dust & blemish
snp3.6:16.4 starts: he has attained the ending of birth:
